@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+//! #2181: the transport line of the stock removal calculated before
+//! playback, and its stamp - an edit of the operation retires the
+//! stored calculation and starts a new one. Provenance: our own
+//! fixtures (a staged face) over the M7.1 field engine.
+//!
+//! Gate map (M4.4): covers ui::play_precalc, ui::actions::ensure_field_view (precalc stamp).
+
+use camcraft_app::commands::{AddTool, CreateOperation, EditOperationParams, GenerateOperation, SetStock};
+use camcraft_app::geometry::{Point3, IDENTITY_Q};
+use camcraft_app::operation::{Height, OpParams, SrcRef};
+use camcraft_app::schema::Location;
+use camcraft_app::stock::StockShape;
+use camcraft_app::stock_play::Precalc;
+use camcraft_app::tools::catalog;
+
+use crate::actions::ensure_field_view;
+use crate::play_precalc::precalc_readout;
+use crate::state::{Sim, State};
+
+fn face(stepover: f64) -> OpParams {
+    OpParams::Face {
+        holes: Default::default(),
+        tilt: None,
+        stepover,
+        clearance_z: Height::fixed(25.0),
+        cut_z: Height::fixed(14.0),
+        top_z: Some(Height::fixed(19.0)),
+        stepdown: Some(2.5),
+        feed: 1200.0,
+        plunge_feed: 300.0,
+        climb: true,
+        blend_turns: false,
+    }
+}
+
+fn faced_state() -> State {
+    let mut state = State::new();
+    let w = &state.world;
+    let loc = Location { pos: Point3::ZERO, rot: IDENTITY_Q };
+    let cmd = SetStock::new(w, StockShape::Box { dx: 12.0, dy: 12.0, dz: 20.0 }, loc).expect("box stock");
+    state.history.execute(w, cmd);
+    let tool = catalog().into_iter().find(|(n, _)| *n == "EM-0400-2FL").map(|(_, t)| t).expect("tool");
+    state.history.execute(w, AddTool::new(w, "EM-0400-2FL", tool).expect("add tool"));
+    let cmd = CreateOperation::new(w, "Face1", "EM-0400-2FL", SrcRef::Stock, face(1.5)).expect("create face");
+    state.history.execute(w, cmd);
+    state.history.execute(w, GenerateOperation::new(w, "Face1").expect("generate"));
+    state.doc_version += 1;
+    state
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn the_readout_says_progress_and_incomplete_and_nothing_when_done() {
+    assert_eq!(precalc_readout(&Precalc::Off), None);
+    let ready = Precalc::Ready { keys: 4, bytes: 1, stride: 64, secs: 0.5 };
+    assert_eq!(precalc_readout(&ready), None, "a finished calculation is not news");
+    let running = precalc_readout(&Precalc::Running { done: 50, total: 200 }).expect("a line");
+    assert!(running.contains("25%"), "{running}");
+    let stopped = Precalc::Incomplete { done: 100, total: 200, why: "cancelled".into() };
+    let line = precalc_readout(&stopped).expect("a line");
+    assert!(line.contains("incomplete") && line.contains("cancelled") && line.contains("50%"), "{line}");
+    let empty = precalc_readout(&Precalc::Running { done: 0, total: 0 }).expect("a line");
+    assert!(empty.contains("100%"), "an empty program does not divide by zero: {empty}");
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn an_edit_of_the_operation_retires_the_stored_calculation() {
+    let mut state = faced_state();
+    state.sim = Some(Sim::new());
+    ensure_field_view(&mut state);
+    let play = state.field_play.as_ref().expect("the transport starts a playback worker");
+    assert_ne!(play.precalc(), Precalc::Off, "the worker calculates before playback");
+    let before = play.index().total();
+    // A frame later, the same document: the same worker stays.
+    ensure_field_view(&mut state);
+    assert_eq!(state.field_play.as_ref().map(|p| p.index().total()), Some(before));
+    // Halve the stepover: more passes, a different program.
+    let w = &state.world;
+    state.history.execute(w, EditOperationParams::new(w, "Face1", face(0.75)).expect("edit"));
+    state.history.execute(w, GenerateOperation::new(w, "Face1").expect("regenerate"));
+    state.doc_version += 1;
+    ensure_field_view(&mut state);
+    let play = state.field_play.as_ref().expect("a new worker for the new program");
+    let after = play.index().total();
+    assert!(after > before, "the stored calculation was for {before} moves; the edited program has {after}");
+    assert_ne!(play.precalc(), Precalc::Off, "and it calculates again");
+}
diff --git a/docs/decisions/2181-sim-precalc.md b/docs/decisions/2181-sim-precalc.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..442e210a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2181-sim-precalc.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+## #2181 - The stock removal of playback is calculated before playback
+
+**Decided.** When the transport starts the traced playback, the
+playback worker first cuts the whole program once. It keeps keyframes of
+the cut stock (`FieldPlay` checkpoints) at a fixed stride. After that,
+each playhead position is shown from the keyframe at or before it, plus
+at most one stride of cutting. A jump forward or back never cuts the
+program again.
+
+- **Where:** in the existing playback worker (`stock_play_worker`), at
+  the first Play of a document version. No new thread, no new cache.
+- **Stamp:** `State::doc_version`. Each command increments it, so an
+  edit of an operation, a tool, the stock, a fixture or a setup retires
+  the worker and its keyframes (the worker is dropped and its thread is
+  joined). An operation delete is a command too: the keyframes are freed
+  with the worker. A stale calculation cannot be shown.
+- **Memory:** a budget of 512 MiB of keyframe cut layers
+  (`PRECALC_BUDGET`), at most 1024 keyframes (`MAX_KEYFRAMES`), at least
+  64 moves between keyframes (`MIN_STRIDE`). Past the budget the store
+  thins: every second keyframe goes and the stride doubles. At worst only
+  the uncut stock stays and playback cuts live, as before.
+- **Cancel and failure:** the transport shows the progress and a Cancel
+  button. A cancel, a stop or a refused cut gives `Precalc::Incomplete`
+  with the reason, and the line says "incomplete". The keyframes made
+  before the stop are exact prefixes of the program, so they stay. The
+  moves after the last keyframe are cut live.
+- **Display only:** the keyframes feed only the playback picture. The
+  Deviate verdict and the post gate (`posting::verification_gate`) are
+  calculated elsewhere and do not change. A test pins the gate result
+  before and after a calculation.
+
+**Why.** The field engine cuts order-free: a prefix of the program is
+cut exactly by its own moves. A keyframe plus the remaining moves is
+therefore bit-identical to the live cut (pinned at every position on a
+small face). The checkpoint store and its backward restore existed; the
+change adds the calculation pass, a forward restore, a byte budget and
+the state readout. This is the smallest change that removes the lag of
+a long jump without a second simulation path.
+
+**Dropped.**
+- One stored state for each move: memory grows with the program; a
+  dense face has hundreds of thousands of moves.
+- Copy-on-write sharing of field bricks between keyframes (denser
+  keyframes for the same memory): it changes the simulation crate's
+  storage and is a separate slice.
+- A calculation directly after Generate: it costs time for documents
+  that are never played, and each edit would start it again.
+- Frames shown while the calculation runs: the worker serves no request
+  until the calculation ends (the sheet stands, the line shows the
+  progress). Serving frames during the calculation needs a second field.
+- Pausing the transport until the calculation ends: the transport keeps
+  its own clock; the picture follows when the calculation is done.
+
+**Cost to change later.** The budget and the keyframe count are
+constants in `crates/app/src/stock_play_precalc.rs`. Moving the start to
+Generate needs only a different call site of `PlayWorker::spawn_precalc`.

From dd90ab9af5519e282de63517208e82a53e3ee31d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:50:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(sim): keep the keyframe budget after a cancel; move
 the store to sim

Review fixes for PR #2192:
- The keyframe store (camcraft_sim::play_keys::Keyframes) has one
  insertion path, offer. The calculation and the live seek both use it,
  so the byte budget and the thinning also hold when live playback seeks
  after a cancel. Pinned by a_live_seek_after_a_cancel_keeps_the_byte_budget.
- The store, Precalc and the calculation loop (play_precalc::drive) move
  to camcraft-sim; app keeps the methods of FieldPlay and PlayWorker and
  re-exports the sim items. The full move of those types is #2268.
- The transport row draws through precalc_row; structural kittest tests
  check the progress text, Cancel, the incomplete text and no row when
  ready, and the shell draws the row from a live worker.

Refs #2181

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
